````gitignore
# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Virtual environment
.venv/
venv/

# Test artifacts
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Environment variables and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local databases and application state
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Generated reports
reports/*.json
reports/*.pdf
cyberrakshak_test_report.pdf

# Local evaluation output
url_evaluation_results.csv

# Backup files
* - backup.py

# Editor and operating system files
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

### 2. Save the file

Press **Ctrl + S**.

### Why these changes matter

| Change | Reason |
|---|---|
| `*.db` | Prevents publishing local scan history |
| `*.sqlite` and `*.sqlite3` | Excludes other local database files |
| `url_evaluation_results.csv` | Keeps generated evaluation output out of the repository |
| `* - backup.py` | Excludes backup files |
| `!.env.example` | Allows a sample environment configuration without secrets |

**Important:** `.gitignore` only prevents untracked files from being added automatically. It does not remove files already tracked by Git.

